BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cloud Native Mexico City|Cloud Native CDMX - Modern Network Automa
 tion with eBPF + AI-Driven Platform Engineering|México|
DTSTART:20260728T160000
CATEGORIES:ai,cloud,devops,frontend,web
DESCRIPTION:🚀 ¡Cloud Native CDMX está de vuelta! Séptima edición de
  nuestro capítulo.\nSeguimos construyendo comunidad Cloud Native en Ciuda
 d de México con una nueva noche de aprendizaje\, networking y tecnología
 .\n📅 28 de julio de 2026\n🕖 16:00 - 20:00 hrs (CST)\n📍 C. Montes 
 Urales 445\, Lomas de Chapultepec\, Ciudad de México\n🎟️ ¡Entrada c
 ompletamente gratuita!\nEsta sesión contará con una ponencia de alto niv
 el técnico:\n🎤\nModern Network Automation with eBPF\, Cilium\, and Ter
 raform in GCP (Google Cloud Platform)\nby\nCamila Martins\nDescubre cómo 
 Cilium y eBPF están revolucionando el networking en Kubernetes\, especial
 mente cuando se integran con Terraform. En esta charla exploraremos cómo 
 automatizar políticas de red avanzadas\, fortalecer la seguridad y mejora
 r la observabilidad a través de Infrastructure as Code (IaC).\nCon ejempl
 os prácticos\, aprenderás a:\nDesplegar clústeres de Kubernetes con con
 figuraciones de red modernas\nConfigurar Cilium y aprovechar eBPF para net
 working dinámico y de alto rendimiento\nAutomatizar políticas de red y m
 ejorar la observabilidad con Hubble\nEscalar y gestionar infraestructuras 
 modernas de forma eficiente\nDiseñada para ingenieros DevOps y entusiasta
 s del ecosistema Cloud Native\, esta sesión te dará insights sobre cómo
  estas herramientas de vanguardia pueden optimizar tu flujo de trabajo y e
 levar tu arquitectura de red.\n🎤\nAI-Driven Platform Engineering: del o
 ncall reactivo al sistema autónomo\nby\nAlejandro Parra\nDescubre cómo l
 a inteligencia artificial está transformando la ingeniería de plataforma
 s\, llevándonos de guardias reactivas y alertas interminables hacia siste
 mas que se auto-diagnostican\, auto-reparan y escalan de forma autónoma. 
 En esta charla exploraremos cómo integrar agentes de IA\, protocolos como
  MCP/A2A y herramientas de observabilidad para construir plataformas que o
 peran de manera inteligente.\nCon ejemplos prácticos\, aprenderás a:\nDi
 señar plataformas self-service que incorporan IA para la detección y res
 olución proactiva de incidentes\nImplementar agentes autónomos que inter
 actúan con tu infraestructura Kubernetes mediante protocolos MCP y A2A\nI
 ntegrar pipelines de observabilidad inteligente con Prometheus\, Grafana y
  modelos de lenguaje para correlación de eventos\nEvolucionar tu modelo o
 perativo: de runbooks manuales a sistemas de auto-remediación impulsados 
 por IA\nDiseñada para ingenieros de plataforma\, SREs y entusiastas del e
 cosistema Cloud Native\, esta sesión te dará una hoja de ruta clara para
  transformar tus operaciones y construir la próxima generación de plataf
 ormas autónomas.\n🔗 Regístrate aquí:\nhttps://ocgroups.dev/cncf/grou
 p/e5vgp72/event/9vuzska\nCloud Native CDMX sigue creciendo con la misión 
 de construir una comunidad técnica sólida\, inclusiva y apasionada por e
 l ecosistema Cloud Native en México.\n¡Sé parte de la comunidad! 🙌
LOCATION:C. Montes Urales 445\, Mexico City
X-CRONQUILES-ADDRESS:C. Montes Urales 445\, Mexico City
X-CRONQUILES-COUNTRY:México
X-CRONQUILES-COUNTRY-CODE:MX
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup|July
  29 - MCP\, Agents and Skills Meetup|Online
DTSTART:20260729T100000
CATEGORIES:ai,data,devops,frontend
DESCRIPTION:México City AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\
 nJoin our virtual meetup to hear talks from experts on cutting-edge topics
  across MCP\, Agents and Skills.\n\n**Date\, Time and Location**\n\nJul 29
 \, 2026\n9:00 AM - 11:00 AM PST\nOnline. **[Register for the Zoom!](https:
 //voxel51.com/events/mcp-agents-skills-meetup-july-29-2026)**\n\n**The Age
 nt Control Plane: Turning Coding Agents into Reliable Engineering Workflow
 s**\n\nAI coding agents are powerful but often unreliable — they halluci
 nate\, lose context\, and produce inconsistent results across runs. In thi
 s talk\, Alex introduces Atomic\, an open-source control plane that adds p
 ersistent memory\, deterministic workflow phases (Research → Specify →
  Implement → Ship)\, and human-in-the-loop gates around coding agents li
 ke Claude Code and GitHub Copilot. The result: repeatable\, auditable engi
 neering workflows that teams can actually trust in production.\n\n*About t
 he Speaker*\n\n[Alex Lavaee](https://www.linkedin.com/in/alexlavaee/) is a
 n Applied AI engineer at Microsoft Research and the creator of Atomic\, an
  open-source SDK that wraps deterministic\, research-to-execution workflow
 s around AI coding agents. He previously conducted AI research at Harvard 
 Medical School and Boston University\, and has worked as an MLE and data s
 cientist at companies including Boeing and Themis AI\, an MIT CSAIL spinof
 f.\n\n**UISurf: Toward Universal UI Automation with Cross-Environment Agen
 ts**\n\nIn this talk\, we introduce UISurf\, an open-source multimodal age
 ntic UI automation platform in which agents can perceive\, reason\, and co
 llaborate across browser and desktop environments to complete end-to-end t
 asks that require interaction with multiple user interfaces.\n\nUISurf com
 prises three main components: uisurf-agent\, the runtime for UI automation
  agents\; uisurf-admin\, the session orchestration and management service\
 ; and uisurf-app\, the full-stack user application. Its multi-agent archit
 ecture includes a planning_agent that transforms natural-language requests
  into structured execution plans\, specialized Browser and Desktop Agents 
 for environment-specific interaction\, an automation_agent that coordinate
 s execution and inter-agent handoff through Agent-to-Agent (A2A) communica
 tion\, and a summarization_agent that produces the final task summary for 
 the user. UISurf supports both autonomous execution and human-in-the-loop 
 supervision\, offering a practical and extensible framework for studying a
 nd deploying cross-environment UI automation.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[D
 r. Henry Ruiz](https://www.linkedin.com/in/haruiz/) is a Research Scientis
 t at Texas A&M University @ AgriLife Research\, specializing in Artificial
  Intelligence (AI) and Remote Sensing. His work focuses on the development
  of advanced software systems and computational algorithms for analyzing m
 ulti-source remote sensing data\, including satellite imagery\, UAVs (Unma
 nned Aerial Vehicles)\, LiDAR (Light Detection and Ranging)\, and Ground P
 enetrating Radar (GPR).\n\n**From Manual Workflows to AI-Assisted Skills: 
 Building Reliable Internal Automation**\n\nIn this session\, I will discus
 s how teams can turn repetitive manual workflows into reliable AI-assisted
  and automation-driven “skills.” I will share practical lessons from b
 uilding internal tools for CAD and engineering workflows\, including how a
 utomation can reduce manual effort\, improve consistency\, and support bet
 ter process control. The talk will also cover why many AI/agent experiment
 s fail when they are not connected to real team workflows\, standards\, an
 d validation steps. Attendees will walk away with a practical framework fo
 r identifying repeatable workflows\, designing useful internal tools\, and
  adopting AI assistance without losing accuracy or trust.\n\n*About the Sp
 eaker*\n\n[Janvi Vijaykumar Saddi](https://voxel51.com/events/www.linkedin
 .com/in/janvi-saddi) \\- Janvi Saddi is a Computer Science graduate and CA
 D/Data Automation professional with experience in data center design workf
 lows\, AutoCAD automation\, process improvement\, and data analytics\\. Sh
 e currently works as a CAD Tech 2 at Astreya\, supporting Google data cent
 er design workflows by building internal tools that reduce manual effort\,
  improve accuracy\, and streamline engineering processes\\. Her background
  also includes SQL\, Power BI\, market research analytics\, and AI\\-assis
 ted development\\.\n\n**Building Safe Agent Sandboxes: Let Agents Act With
 out Breaking Production**\n\nAI agents become truly useful when they can t
 ake action\, not just generate text. But giving agents access to code\, da
 ta\, and systems raises an important question: how do you let them explore
 \, execute\, fail\, and improve without putting production at risk?\n\nIn 
 this talk\, we'll explore the sandbox pattern for agent systems and how to
  equip agents with tools to read\, write\, execute\, and iterate within co
 ntrolled environments while using permissions\, human approval\, and safet
 y guardrails to keep them reliable. We'll cover practical architectures an
 d lessons learned for building agents that can safely evolve from experime
 ntation to production..\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Adonai Vera](https://ww
 w.linkedin.com/in/adonai-vera/) \\- Adonai Vera \\- Machine Learning Engin
 eer & DevRel at Voxel51\\. With over 7 years of experience building comput
 er vision and machine learning models using TensorFlow\, Docker\, and Open
 CV\\.
LOCATION:Online event\,
END:VEVENT
